{
	title: 'Left-filled usage bars in both clients',
	spec: '/status usage bars in web and terminal use the same 14-character meter that fills left to right: full blocks (█), then at most one partial block that fills from the bottom up (▁▂▃▄▅▆▇), then ░ for the empty track. The shared Markdown parser marks such a run (two or more characters) as a meter; both clients draw the empty track and the space above the partial block on a dim background (terminal: fg mixed 25% into bg; web: currentColor at 25%), and ░ shows as blank there. Monochrome terminals and plain text keep the ░ characters. Zero usage is an empty track; positive usage rounds up to an eighth of a cell so low usage stays visible; percentages clamp to 0..100. This replaces filling every cell upward at once (bar height showed usage). Numeric percentages, reset labels, tables and all other behavior remain unchanged.',
	status: 'done',
